prije, pensycertu

----

''tsajmi'' 'strong understand', as opposed to 'weak-understand' ''rubjmi'' ("stupid"). ''prije'' means 'wise' as opposed to ''bebna'' 'foolish'. And ''pensi'' 'think about' is closer to "contemplate" than some process of ratiocination. "Analyze" might be conveyed by ''ckiski'' 'explainingly-describe'. But Lojbanic psychology is still in its infancy...

----

''banzu jinvi''

When I say "intelligent", I often mean ''menstati'', "mentally talented". ''mi'e ((jezrax))''
